reference/generators:
Generator functions use `fn*` and `yield` to produce values lazily.

```xs
fn* count_up(n) {
    var i = 0
    while i < n {
        yield i
        i = i + 1
    }
}

for x in count_up(5) {
    print("{x} ")                -- 0 1 2 3 4
}
```

Generators pause at each `yield` and resume when the next value is requested. They work with `for..in` loops.

